From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: grf53 <grf0503@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:22:21 +0900
Subject: virgl-renderer: virgl_renderer on Windows: no render node, export_blob unsupported

## Why virtx needs it

A Windows host's GPU is venus, which virglrenderer serves and libkrun reaches through rutabaga_gfx.
rutabaga's `virgl_renderer.rs` is written for a POSIX host, and did not build on Windows.

## What it changes

The patch is Windows-only. `virgl_renderer.rs` opens a DRM render node, folds
stderr into stdout with `dup2`, and turns exported `int` fds into descriptors —
none of which exist on Windows. On Windows `export_blob` has to report `Unsupported`, since a
`RawDescriptor` is a `HANDLE` that does not fit in the `int` virglrenderer
exports blobs through. `map()` needs nothing: virglrenderer maps a blob there
by lending the venus context's own pointer.

## When it can go

When upstream virglrenderer serves venus on Windows and upstream rutabaga_gfx builds against it there.
